<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:AgIO.Views"
        x:Class="AgIO.Views.FormISOBUS"
        x:DataType="vm:FormISOBUSViewModel"
        Title="ISOBUS"
        RequestedThemeVariant="Light"
        Background="Gainsboro"
        Width="660" Height="540"
        MinWidth="560" MinHeight="420"
        CanResize="True"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        SystemDecorations="Full"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="14.25">
    <!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms FormISOBUS.cs + FormISOBUS.Designer.cs — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
    <!--
        [XPLAT] Avalonia 1:1 PARITY reimplementation of the deleted WinForms AgIO "ISOBUS" dialog
        (Forms/FormISOBUS.Designer.cs + Forms/FormISOBUS.cs + FormISOBUS.resx). Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a
        visual/behavioral PARITY rebuild of the current Windows Forms look — never a redesign. It lets the
        operator pick a CAN adapter + channel and Open/Close the external AOG-TaskController (the AOG Task
        Controller), with an OK / Cancel command bar.

        Bound via COMPILED bindings (x:DataType="vm:FormISOBUSViewModel") to FormISOBUSViewModel. The
        view-model owns ALL logic — the adapter/channel lists, the Windows-only Registry install lookup and
        Process launch/stop (both fenced behind #if WINDOWS), and settings persistence
        (isobus_canAdapterIndex / isobus_canChannelIndex / isobus_isOn). This view only data-binds; it
        declares no event handlers. The dialog outcome is surfaced by the code-behind
        (FormISOBUS.axaml.cs) in response to the view-model's RequestClose event — a window concern, not
        declared in this markup.

        Parity mapping (WinForms FormISOBUS.Designer.cs / FormISOBUS.cs  ->  Avalonia):
          • Form Text "ISOBUS Settings" / agent-prompt Title "ISOBUS"  -> Title="ISOBUS".
          • BackColor Gainsboro                                        -> Background="Gainsboro".
          • ClientSize 644x526; textBoxRcv anchored Top|Bottom|Left|   -> Width/Height 660x540,
            Right (=> the form was resizable)                             CanResize="True" + MinWidth/MinHeight.
          • Opened from an owner window                                -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner".
          • Font Tahoma                                                -> FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="14.25".
          • lblCurrentAdapter "CANbus Adapter" (Tahoma 11.25 Bold)     -> bold TextBlock above the adapter combo.
          • cboxRadioAdapter — 4 fixed items, Tahoma 18 Bold,          -> ComboBox cboxRadioAdapter,
            DropDownList                                                  ItemsSource={Binding AdapterNames}
                                                                          (the SAME four entries: PEAK-PCAN /
                                                                          InnoMaker-USB2CAN / Rusoku-TouCAN /
                                                                          SYS-TEC-USB2CAN), SelectedIndex
                                                                          two-way bound to SelectedAdapterIndex.
          • lblChannel "Channel"                                       -> bold TextBlock above the channel combo.
          • cboxRadioChannel — rebuilt to 1..N at runtime by           -> ComboBox cboxRadioChannel,
            UpdateChannelSelection()                                      ItemsSource={Binding ChannelOptions}
                                                                          (dynamic 1..N for the selected adapter),
                                                                          SelectedIndex two-way bound to
                                                                          SelectedChannelIndex.
          • btnOpenIsobus (USB_Connect bitmap)                         -> "Open ISOBUS" button -> OpenIsobusCommand.
          • btnCloseIsobus (USB_Disconnect bitmap)                     -> "Close ISOBUS" button -> CloseIsobusCommand.
          • flowLayoutDownloadIsobus (lblDownloadIsobus + LinkLabel)   -> download prompt shown when ShowDownloadLink.
          • textBoxRcv (read-only, multiline, ScrollBars=Both,         -> read-only multiline TextBox bound
            WordWrap=false, BackColor=Window)                            one-way to LogText.
          • btnIsobusOK (OK64 bitmap; Click -> Hide())                 -> "OK" button -> OkCommand (IsDefault).
          • (the WinForms form had no Cancel; the VM adds one)         -> "Cancel" button -> CancelCommand (IsCancel).

        Buttons render as TEXT, not the WinForms OK64 / USB_Connect / USB_Disconnect bitmaps: the migrated
        AgIO.csproj registers NO btnImages assets as <AvaloniaResource> (only GPS/AgOpenGPS.csproj does) and
        excludes Properties/Resources.Designer.cs from compilation (System.Drawing purged). Referencing
        avares://AgIO/btnImages/* here would NOT resolve and would render a broken image — so, consistent
        with every sibling AgIO view (FormYes / FormSource / FormPGN / FormRadioChannel), affordances are
        text. See MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md.

        Windows feature-gate (AAP §0.6.3 / §0.7.2 graceful degradation): launching the AOG-TaskController is
        Windows-only. The view-model's IsSupported is true only on Windows, so the Open/Close buttons bind
        IsEnabled="{Binding IsSupported}" and are disabled on Linux/macOS, where the "Available on Windows
        only" hint is shown instead (IsVisible="{Binding !IsSupported}", Avalonia compiled-binding boolean
        negation). The adapter panel, the download prompt and the log are driven by the view-model's
        ShowAdapterPanel / ShowDownloadLink / ShowLog flags, reproducing the WinForms
        UpdateComponentVisibility() show/hide split.

        Theme: Light only — App.axaml pins RequestedThemeVariant="Light" (AgIO has no day/night toggle);
        restated here for explicitness (mirrors FormSource / FormPGN).
    -->
    <DockPanel Margin="12" LastChildFill="True">

        <!-- Bottom command bar. Cancel sits to the LEFT of OK so OK stays right-aligned (the WinForms
             btnIsobusOK was bottom-right; the view-model adds an explicit Cancel). Text affordances,
             touch-friendly (>= 44px). IsDefault maps Enter to OK; IsCancel maps Escape to Cancel. The
             actual window close is performed by the code-behind in response to the view-model's
             RequestClose event (a window concern, not declared here). -->
        <StackPanel DockPanel.Dock="Bottom"
                    Orientation="Horizontal"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                    VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                    Spacing="12"
                    Margin="0,12,0,0">
            <Button x:Name="btnCancel"
                    Content="Cancel"
                    Command="{Binding CancelCommand}"
                    IsCancel="True"
                    Width="96" Height="64"
                    MinWidth="64" MinHeight="44"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel" />
            <Button x:Name="btnIsobusOK"
                    Content="OK"
                    Command="{Binding OkCommand}"
                    IsDefault="True"
                    Width="101" Height="64"
                    MinWidth="64" MinHeight="44"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="OK" />
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- "Available on Windows only" hint — shown ONLY when the platform cannot launch the task
             controller (Linux / macOS). IsVisible uses Avalonia's compiled-binding boolean negation of
             IsSupported (the view-model exposes no IsNotSupported flag). On Windows IsSupported is true,
             so this collapses and the adapter panel / download prompt / log are shown instead. -->
        <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                   Text="Available on Windows only"
                   IsVisible="{Binding !IsSupported}"
                   FontWeight="Bold"
                   FontSize="16"
                   Foreground="#555555"
                   TextWrapping="Wrap"
                   HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                   Margin="0,8,0,12"
                   AutomationProperties.Name="ISOBUS availability notice" />

        <!-- Download prompt (WinForms flowLayoutDownloadIsobus): shown when the platform supports the
             feature but the task controller is not installed (ShowDownloadLink). The label and URL are
             frozen reference text reproduced verbatim from the WinForms lblDownloadIsobus / linkDownloadIsobus.
             The URL is rendered as a selectable styled text line — opening a browser is a code-behind
             concern, deliberately kept out of this declarative view (no Process dependency in the markup). -->
        <StackPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                    IsVisible="{Binding ShowDownloadLink}"
                    Orientation="Vertical"
                    Spacing="2"
                    Margin="0,0,0,12">
            <TextBlock Text="AOG-TaskController not installed, please download from:"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       FontSize="11.25"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap" />
            <SelectableTextBlock Text="https://github.com/GwnDaan/AOG-TaskController"
                                 FontWeight="Bold"
                                 FontSize="11.25"
                                 Foreground="#1A0DAB"
                                 TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                 AutomationProperties.Name="AOG-TaskController download URL" />
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- Adapter / Channel selection + Open/Close (WinForms flowLayoutCANAdapter + flowLayoutChannel +
             btnOpenIsobus + btnCloseIsobus). Shown when the task controller is installed (ShowAdapterPanel).
             The combos are disabled while the process runs (IsAdapterSelectionEnabled), reproducing the
             WinForms enable/disable. Open/Close bind IsEnabled to IsSupported per the agent-prompt; their
             commands' CanExecute additionally gate installed/running, so on Windows exactly one is
             actionable at a time (Open when stopped, Close when running) — the functional equivalent of the
             WinForms show/hide of the two buttons. -->
        <StackPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                    IsVisible="{Binding ShowAdapterPanel}"
                    Orientation="Horizontal"
                    Spacing="16"
                    Margin="0,0,0,8">

            <!-- WinForms flowLayoutCANAdapter: lblCurrentAdapter "CANbus Adapter" + cboxRadioAdapter. -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="2">
                <TextBlock Text="CANbus Adapter"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           FontSize="11.25"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                <ComboBox x:Name="cboxRadioAdapter"
                          ItemsSource="{Binding AdapterNames}"
                          SelectedIndex="{Binding SelectedAdapterIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          IsEnabled="{Binding IsAdapterSelectionEnabled}"
                          Width="221"
                          MinHeight="37"
                          FontSize="18"
                          FontWeight="Bold"
                          VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                          AutomationProperties.Name="CANbus adapter" />
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- WinForms flowLayoutChannel: lblChannel "Channel" + cboxRadioChannel (dynamic 1..N items). -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="2">
                <TextBlock Text="Channel"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           FontSize="11.25"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                <ComboBox x:Name="cboxRadioChannel"
                          ItemsSource="{Binding ChannelOptions}"
                          SelectedIndex="{Binding SelectedChannelIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          IsEnabled="{Binding IsAdapterSelectionEnabled}"
                          Width="116"
                          MinHeight="37"
                          FontSize="18"
                          FontWeight="Bold"
                          VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                          AutomationProperties.Name="CAN channel" />
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- WinForms btnOpenIsobus (USB_Connect bitmap). Enabled only on Windows (IsSupported); the
                 command's CanExecute (CanOpenTaskController) further requires installed + not-running. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnOpenIsobus"
                    Content="Open ISOBUS"
                    Command="{Binding OpenIsobusCommand}"
                    IsEnabled="{Binding IsSupported}"
                    Width="120" Height="58"
                    MinHeight="44"
                    VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Open ISOBUS" />

            <!-- WinForms btnCloseIsobus (USB_Disconnect bitmap). Enabled only on Windows (IsSupported); the
                 command's CanExecute (CanCloseTaskController) further requires the process to be running. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnCloseIsobus"
                    Content="Close ISOBUS"
                    Command="{Binding CloseIsobusCommand}"
                    IsEnabled="{Binding IsSupported}"
                    Width="120" Height="58"
                    MinHeight="44"
                    VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Close ISOBUS" />
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- Process output log (WinForms textBoxRcv): read-only, multiline, no word-wrap, both scrollbars,
             white background; shown when the task controller is installed (ShowLog). This is the DockPanel
             last child, so it fills the remaining space. Bound one-way to LogText (the view-model appends
             the task-controller process output on Windows; it stays empty on other platforms). -->
        <TextBox x:Name="textBoxRcv"
                 Text="{Binding LogText, Mode=OneWay}"
                 IsReadOnly="True"
                 AcceptsReturn="True"
                 TextWrapping="NoWrap"
                 IsVisible="{Binding ShowLog}"
                 Background="White"
                 FontFamily="Tahoma"
                 FontSize="11.25"
                 FontWeight="Bold"
                 ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                 ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                 AutomationProperties.Name="ISOBUS task controller log" />
    </DockPanel>
</Window>
